      "history": {
        "title": "Firearm Origin...",
        "content": "The Savage Axis is a modern bolt-action rifle introduced by Savage Arms as an affordable and reliable platform for hunting and general shooting. Designed with simplicity and function as priorities, the Axis emphasizes ease of use, durability, and consistent accuracy at an accessible price point.\n\nThe rifle features a push-feed bolt-action system with dual locking lugs and Savage’s floating bolt head design, which helps ensure even lug engagement and contributes to accuracy. It is commonly chambered in popular hunting calibers such as .308 Winchester and .30-06 Springfield.\n\nA lightweight synthetic stock and detachable box magazine make the Axis well-suited for field use. Many models are factory-drilled and tapped for optics, reflecting its role as a practical hunting rifle rather than a military or historical firearm.\n\nAlthough positioned as an entry-level rifle, the Axis benefits from Savage’s reputation for precision manufacturing. Many examples are capable of sub-MOA accuracy with appropriate ammunition.\n\nToday, the Savage Axis is widely used by hunters and recreational shooters seeking a dependable, no-frills rifle that delivers strong performance without unnecessary complexity.",
        "wikipedia": {
          "title": "",
