      "history": {
        "title": "Firearm Origin...",
        "content": "The MAS-49/56 chambered in 7.5×54mm French represents the original military configuration of France’s standard post-war service rifle. Developed from earlier MAS designs, it combined semi-automatic fire with a robust and reliable operating system suited to mid-20th century warfare.\n\nThe rifle utilizes a direct impingement gas system and a tilting bolt, providing consistent cycling and durability. It was designed to be compact and versatile, incorporating features such as grenade launching capability and durable iron sights.\n\nUnlike later converted variants, the original 7.5 French chambering reflects the rifle’s intended ballistic performance and military role. The cartridge provided effective range and stopping power comparable to other full-power service cartridges of the era.\n\nThe MAS-49/56 saw extensive service in French military operations and remained in use until replaced by more modern designs.\n\nToday, rifles in original 7.5 French configuration are particularly valued by collectors for their authenticity and historical significance.",
