      "history": {
        "title": "Firearm Origin...",
        "content": "The AR-10 is a full-power battle rifle platform originally developed in the 1950s and later produced by numerous manufacturers, including Palmetto State Armory. Chambered in 7.62×51mm NATO (.308 Winchester), it offers increased range and stopping power compared to smaller-caliber rifles.\n\nLike the AR-15, the AR-10 uses a gas-operated system and features a modular design that allows extensive customization. Components such as barrels, handguards, and optics can be easily adapted to suit specific applications.\n\nPalmetto State Armory produces AR-10 style rifles aimed at balancing affordability with modern performance. These rifles are commonly used for hunting, precision shooting, and general-purpose applications.\n\nThe platform retains the ergonomic advantages of the AR family while delivering the ballistic performance of a full-power rifle cartridge.\n\nToday, AR-10 rifles are valued for their versatility, accuracy, and adaptability across a wide range of shooting disciplines.",
        "wikipedia": {
          "title": "ArmaLite AR-10",
          "content": "The ArmaLite AR-10 is a 7.62×51mm NATO battle rifle designed by Eugene Stoner in the late 1950s and manufactured by ArmaLite (then a division of the Fairchild Aircraft Corporation).",
