    "tabs": {
      "history": {
        "title": "Firearm Origin...",
        "content": "The Springfield Armory M1A is a civilian semi-automatic rifle derived from the U.S. military’s M14 rifle, itself an evolution of the M1 Garand. Chambered in 7.62×51mm NATO (.308 Winchester), the M1A combines traditional rifle design with modern performance.\n\nThe rifle operates using a gas system with a rotating bolt, providing reliable cycling and durability. It is typically fed from detachable box magazines and is known for its accuracy and effective range.\n\nThe M1A retains classic features such as a traditional stock and iron sights while supporting modern optics and accessories. This blend of old and new has contributed to its enduring popularity among civilian shooters.\n\nWidely used in competition shooting, hunting, and recreational marksmanship, the M1A is particularly valued for its precision at extended distances.\n\nToday, the M1A represents a continuation of America’s service rifle lineage, offering shooters a historically rooted platform with modern capabilities.",
        "wikipedia": {
          "title": "Springfield Armory M1A",
          "content": "The Springfield Armory M1A is a semi-automatic rifle made by Springfield Armory, Inc., beginning in 1971, based on the M14 rifle, for the civilian and law enforcement markets in the United States. \"M1A\" is a proprietary name for Springfield Armory's M14-pattern rifle.",
          "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Springfield_Armory_M1A"
        },
        "gunDigest": {
          "title": "Springfield Armory M1A: The M14 Soldiers On",
          "content": "While the short service life of the M14 should have made it a military footnote, the design remains as popular as ever thanks in part to the Springfield Armory M1A.",
          "url": "https://gundigest.com/article/springfield-armory-m1a-the-m14-soldiers-on"
        }
      },
