    "tabs": {
      "history": {
        "title": "Firearm Origin...",
        "content": "The CVA Wolf is a modern in-line muzzleloading rifle designed for simplicity, reliability, and accessibility, particularly for hunters participating in black powder seasons. Manufactured by Connecticut Valley Arms (CVA), the Wolf represents an evolution of traditional muzzleloading firearms adapted to modern materials and ignition systems.\n\nChambered in .50 caliber, the rifle is loaded from the muzzle using loose black powder or modern substitutes such as Pyrodex or Triple Seven, along with a projectile such as a sabot bullet or conical lead projectile. Unlike historical flintlock or percussion rifles, the Wolf uses a 209 shotgun primer ignition system, providing more consistent and reliable ignition in a wide range of weather conditions.\n\nThe rifle features a break-action design that allows easy access to the breech plug for cleaning and maintenance, a significant improvement over traditional muzzleloaders. Its synthetic stock and stainless or blued steel barrel contribute to durability and resistance to environmental conditions encountered during hunting seasons.\n\nThe CVA Wolf is typically equipped with fiber optic sights and is also compatible with optics, reflecting its intended use as a practical hunting tool rather than a historical reproduction. It is widely used for deer hunting in regions where muzzleloader seasons are regulated separately from standard firearm seasons.\n\nWhile retaining the fundamental loading method of traditional muzzleloading rifles, the Wolf incorporates modern engineering to improve ease of use, safety, and reliability.\n\nToday, the CVA Wolf is regarded as an entry-level yet capable muzzleloader, offering hunters an accessible way to participate in black powder hunting with the benefits of contemporary firearm design.",
